<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Flowchart depicting an audio analysis process: audio and a spectrogram are preprocessed, generating a mel spectrogram for CNN-based deep feature extraction and handcrafted features via opensmile and mRMR analysis.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustrating a two-stage neural network pipeline: Stage 1 fuses Mel spectrograms and acoustic features using a transformer attention mechanism; Stage 2 performs depression, emotion, and gender recognition using convolutional, pooling, and fully connected layers with auxiliary tasks feeding intermediate representations.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Horizontal bar chart showing types of acoustic features and their counts, grouped by categories: Spectrum, F0, Energy, Formant, and Voice quality. MFCC has the highest count at thirty.) /K 1 /P 9 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Two scatter plots compare data point separation before and after fusion in a classification task, with blue triangles representing depression and pink crosses representing normal. Before fusion, clusters overlap significantly. After fusion, depression and normal groups are more distinctly separated.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
